            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this review the therapeutical options of physiotherapy in patients with chronic musculoskeletal pain, especially non-specific back pain, are reported. The importance of the objective &quot;reduction of pain related disability of individual activities of daily living&quot; is reported. Various methods of exercise therapy and their application in either a monodisciplinary setting or in an interdisciplinary pain management team are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
